WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.240 position:64%
A top CEO and her security team
were dining at this Copenhagen restaurant

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.200 position:64%
when they noticed something
unsettling outside the 17th floor window.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.800 position:58%
A drone seemed to be monitoring them.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.840 position:56%
They had good reason to be paranoid.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.320 position:61%
They were here celebrating the end of a
two-and-a-half month investigation

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.040 position:56%
that found that the Chinese company,
Huawei, had conducted this hamfisted

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.560
espionage effort to try to
secure a $200 million contract.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.400 position:56%
This was about more than just money.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.466 position:58%
Telecoms networks are a critical part
of any country's national security.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:37.240 position:59%
The investigation revealed
the extent of the alleged dirty tricks

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.320
that a Chinese tech giant
would deploy to get a piece of it.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.760 position:59%
It all started in early 2019
here at the headquarters of TDC Group.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.080 position:58%
It's Denmark's biggest telecoms firm.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.520
It's also where the team
dining at Restaurant Silo worked.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.120
At the time, this was early 2019,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.480
TDC had a tender offer out there
for a contract worth

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.000
more than $200 million
to build their 5G telecoms network.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.280
And at that time they had whittled
down the bidders to just two:

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.400 position:58%
Sweden's Ericsson and China's Huawei.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.497
The details in those tender
offers are

00:01:28.497 --> 00:01:30.873
very closely protected,
things like pricing.

00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:32.640
How much do you charge for things?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.800
Ericsson, as it turns out,
had offered to do this job

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.320 position:58%
for less money than Huawei;
Huawei was not supposed to know that.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.440
Huawei somehow found out.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.920 position:63%
And just hours before the final decision

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.240
And in fact, its bid
was slightly lower than Ericsson's.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.760
How had the information managed
to seep out?

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.840 position:59%
TDC called an emergency investigation.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.720
Within that decade,
Huawei had leapfrogged

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.160
other rivals,
including Ericsson and Nokia,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.560
to become the world's biggest maker
of telecommunications equipment.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.480 position:61%
While not as big as Tencent or Alibaba,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.960 position:61%
Huawei is a far more successful Chinese
tech export.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.040
The company says that its
technology connects

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.200 position:61%
over 3 billion people in 170 countries.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.560 position:58%
The way they did that was not without
its controversies, right?

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.520 position:64%
For many years, Huawei has been under
suspicion by the US government and others

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.960 position:61%
for potentially being under the control
of the Chinese government.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.120 position:61%
We start with the Biden administration,
which is said to be considering

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.520
cutting Huawei off
from all of its American suppliers.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.160
Huawei is a bad actor.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.600
There's a lot of intelligence
suggesting that they're very close

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.760
to the Chinese military
and to Chinese intel.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.320
So controversy has followed Huawei
wherever it's gone.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.120
But here in Denmark,
Huawei was a trusted provider,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:59.080 position:59%
Huawei had worked with TDC since 2013,
so for many years, Huawei had supplied

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.360
the key equipment that TDC
used for its 3G and 4G networks.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.400 position:64%
Huawei had an office on this campus
and many of its engineers badged into TDC

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.680 position:63%
every single day to service the network,

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.200
it was seen as a trusted provider.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.840
TDC becomes
very alarmed because it's clear

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.280
that somebody has leaked to Huawei
Ericsson's sensitive information.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.520
TDC begins an investigation
focused on potential insiders,

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.720 position:58%
potential hacking, and also potential
eavesdropping within their offices.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.680 position:66%
And in fact, a sweep of the boardroom
found microphones hidden in the boardroom.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.240 position:66%
These are some of the most sensitive types
of investigations because in this case,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.720
maybe five, maybe ten at most,
people had this information.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.160
What did they find?

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.680 position:66%
What they find is that the head of special
projects, a guy named Dov Goldstein,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.440 position:64%
they find very quickly that he had leaked
this information to Huawei.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.480
The investigation
as such was fairly straightforward.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.800
However, when they requested CCTV

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.880
footage of Dov Goldstein's
comings and goings,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.800 position:63%
Dov Goldstein finds out and he confronts
the executive team at TDC.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.480
So there was a leak within
the security investigation.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.920
This heightened
the paranoia even further.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.920
The security team decides
we can't trust our own environment.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.720
We need to leave.
We need to take our evidence.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.680
They seize the executives’ phones.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.840
They seize their laptops.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.520 position:58%
This is a very serious investigation.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.240 position:56%
They realize
we can't hold that information here.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.280
We need to take that evidence
to another place, a secure location

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.760 position:63%
where we can conduct this investigation.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:40.840 position:56%
If you look up there, that big brown
building is the Plesner law firm.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.400
That’s the building where
TDC’s security group

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.800
moved their investigation.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.880
They booked a conference room

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.560 position:59%
on the 15th floor of these law offices
as the secure place

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.120
to conduct the rest
of their investigation.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.000
But it quickly sort of went awry?

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.080 position:73%
That same night that they moved
their investigation from TDC headquarters here,

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:05.040 position:58%
Plesner’s computer network
came under sustained hacking attacks.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.800 position:64%
The next day, after midnight,
a security guard noticed a drone hovering

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.240
outside the same 15th floor window
where the team was working.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.560 position:59%
One of the reasons they saw the drone,
it had lights on it?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.400 position:56%
It apparently had lights, which adds
even more levels of intrigue to it,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.920 position:61%
because if you lit up that room
at that time with the blinds not drawn,

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.320 position:58%
you would have seen the full timeline
of this team's investigation.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.160
The paranoia heightened.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.480
Members of the security team

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.680 position:56%
started to notice the same strangers
popping up around town,

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.440 position:66%
appearing to follow and photograph
them as they ate at restaurants or entered

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.800
and left their homes.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:45.200 position:56%
Even TDC CEO Allison Kirkby seemed
to have attracted a persistent tail.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.360 position:77%
To make matters worse, Huawei
managers had written to the Danish prime minister

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.720
warning that should Huawei not
get the TDC contract,

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:53.440
it would quote,

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.400 position:66%
The prime minister’s office didn’t comment

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.120
The reaction was swift.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.840
Goldstein left the company.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.040
The investigation found he
had allegedly leaked

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:09.280
Ericsson's secret information
to Jason Lan.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.120 position:64%
He led Huawei's operations
in Denmark and, investigators determined,

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.960 position:56%
had essentially cultivated Goldstein
as a source.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.040
He returned to China.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.040
With the investigation
concluded and

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.880 position:61%
alleged source of the leaks identified,

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.760
a celebratory dinner was called.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.120 position:59%
They gathered here at Restaurant Silo.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.160
Allison Kirkby
reflected on the paranoia

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.400 position:66%
that had enveloped them and cracked a joke
about when she'd next see a drone.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.600 position:59%
Minutes later,
a drone reappeared outside the window.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.920 position:56%
The security team watched
as it descended to the street below.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:43.040
Men in a white van grabbed it
and sped away.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.720
And the contract?

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:47.120
Ericsson still won it.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.680
No criminal charges were filed
as a consequence of the affair.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.600
Goldstein declined to comment.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.880
Ericsson declined to comment.

